Well, Phil's a minor league baseball player.


00:19:34.618 --> 00:19:37.581
And he travels a lot.


00:19:37.582 --> 00:19:41.700
- My mom stayed home with me but I
knew it didn't make her happy so...


00:19:42.701 --> 00:19:46.246
I figured I'd stay with
my dad for a while...


00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:49.300
And now you're unhappy.


00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.490
No...


00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:55.133
I'm sorry, I'm just
trying to figure you out.


00:19:55.134 --> 00:19:58.500
You're very difficult for me to read.


00:19:58.501 --> 00:20:00.500
Hey, did you get contacts?


00:20:01.300 --> 00:20:02.100
No.


00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:07.718
Your eyes were black the
last time I saw you and now...


00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:09.900
They're like golden-brown.


00:20:09.901 --> 00:20:10.995
Yeah, I know. It's the... Um,


00:20:12.551 --> 00:20:13.943
it's the fluorescence.


00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.153
- Bella, I'm so sorry...
I panicked.


00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:22.729
Bella! I've got 911 on the phone now.


00:21:28.500 --> 00:21:29.750
Bella,


00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:30.850
are you okay?


00:21:30.900 --> 00:21:32.400
You and I are gonna talk.


00:21:32.401 --> 00:21:34.300
- You alright?
- I'm fine dad, calm down.


00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:36.600
I'm sorry Bella, I tried to stop.


00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:38.200
I know, it's okay.


00:21:38.201 --> 00:21:40.530
No, as sure as hell it's not okay.


00:21:40.700 --> 00:21:42.200
Dad, it wasn't his fault.


00:21:42.201 --> 00:21:44.362
You could've been killed.
You understand that?


00:21:44.363 --> 00:21:46.600
Yes. But I wasn't, so...


00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:49.162
You can kiss your license goodbye.


00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:52.000
I heard the Chief's daughter was in...


00:21:52.001 --> 00:21:53.001
Oh, Dr. Cullen.


00:21:53.002 --> 00:21:54.024
Charlie.


00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:55.934
I got this one, Jackie.


00:21:58.100 --> 00:21:59.200
Isabella.


00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:01.300
Bella.


00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:03.997
- Well, Bella... Looks like it's
a quiet spill. How do you feel?


00:22:03.998 --> 00:22:05.291
Good.


00:22:06.500 --> 00:22:07.600
Look here...


00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:12.900
You might experience some post traumatic
stress or... disorientation but...


00:22:12.901 --> 00:22:14.300
Your vitals are good.


00:22:14.301 --> 00:22:16.400
No signs of any head trauma.


00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:18.500
I think you'll be just fine.


00:22:18.501 --> 00:22:20.700
I'm so sorry Bella, I'm really...


00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:27.500
It would have been a lot worse if Edward
wasn't there. He knocked me out of the way.


00:22:28.400 --> 00:22:31.000
Edward? Your boy?


00:22:31.001 --> 00:22:32.200
Yeah, it was amazing.


00:22:32.201 --> 00:22:35.400
- I mean, he got to me so fast...
He was nowhere near me.


00:22:35.401 --> 00:22:37.200
Sounds like you were very lucky.


00:22:37.600 --> 00:22:38.400
Charlie...


00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:45.300
I need to sign some paperwork...


00:22:46.900 --> 00:22:48.200
You should probably call your mom.


00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:50.261
Did you tell her?


00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:58.097
She's probably just... freaking out.


00:23:00.300 --> 00:23:01.280
...What happened.


00:23:01.300 --> 00:23:03.600
- What was I supposed to do?
Let her die?


00:23:03.601 --> 00:23:06.600
- This isn't just about you.
It's about all of us.


00:23:06.601 --> 00:23:08.600
I think we should talk this in my office...


00:23:11.400 --> 00:23:12.700
Can I talk to you for a minute?


00:23:12.701 --> 00:23:13.516
Rosalie...


00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:21.851
What?


00:23:25.343 --> 00:23:26.813
How did you get over to me so fast?


00:23:27.843 --> 00:23:29.903
I was standing right next to you, Bella.


00:23:30.211 --> 00:23:30.971
No,


00:23:31.594 --> 00:23:34.244
you were next to your car... Across the lot.


00:23:34.813 --> 00:23:35.700
No, I wasn't.


00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:39.868
Yes, you were!


00:23:42.173 --> 00:23:46.900
Bella, you hit your head...
I think you're confused.


00:23:46.901 --> 00:23:48.551
I know what I saw.


00:23:48.552 --> 00:23:50.500
What exactly was that?


00:23:51.873 --> 00:23:56.446
You... You stopped the van.


00:23:57.375 --> 00:23:59.115
You pushed it away with your hand.


00:24:01.008 --> 00:24:02.338
Well, nobody's gonna believe you, so...


00:24:04.971 --> 00:24:06.691
I wasn't gonna tell anybody.


00:24:07.527 --> 00:24:09.417
I just need to know the truth...


00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:13.300
Can't you just thank me and get over it?


00:24:14.100 --> 00:24:15.300
Thank you.


00:24:17.300 --> 00:24:18.653
You're not gonna let this go, are you?


00:24:18.654 --> 00:24:19.800
No.


00:24:20.300 --> 00:24:22.200
Well, then I hope you enjoy disappointment.


00:24:57.600 --> 00:25:00.200
That was the first night I
dreamt with Edward Cullen.


00:25:03.500 --> 00:25:05.900
I need everybody's permission slips, so...


00:25:05.901 --> 00:25:09.500
Let's go!


00:25:24.000 --> 00:25:25.137
Look at you, huh?


00:25:25.138 --> 00:25:27.000
You're alive!


00:25:27.001 --> 00:25:29.500
I know, Yeah... False alarm, I guess.


00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:33.400
Um, now I wanted to ask you, you know...


00:25:33.401 --> 00:25:35.700
If... It's like a month away but...


00:25:37.400 --> 00:25:41.052
Do you wanna go to Prom...?


00:25:44.000 --> 00:25:45.600
So... What do you think?


00:25:46.700 --> 00:25:47.600
About what?


00:25:47.601 --> 00:25:49.100
Do you wanna go...?


00:25:51.200 --> 00:25:52.000
To Prom...?


00:25:52.900 --> 00:25:54.600
With me?


00:25:54.601 --> 00:25:58.900
Oh! I... Prom...


00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:00.900
Dancing...


00:26:01.800 --> 00:26:03.700
Not such a good idea for me.


00:26:05.900 --> 00:26:07.900
I have something that weekend, anyway.


00:26:08.100 --> 00:26:10.300
I'm going to Jacksonville that weekend.


00:26:10.301 --> 00:26:12.300
You can't go another weekend?


00:26:12.301 --> 00:26:13.800
Non-refundable ticket...


00:26:15.000 --> 00:26:16.300
You should ask Jessica.


00:26:17.100 --> 00:26:18.700
I know she wants to go with you.


00:26:22.700 --> 00:26:24.000
Hey guys! Come on!


00:26:24.500 --> 00:26:27.400
- We gotta go, we gotta go!
Green is what?


00:26:27.401 --> 00:26:28.700
Good! Let's go!


00:26:28.701 --> 00:26:30.096
Guys, come on!


00:26:31.700 --> 00:26:33.300
- Other bus... Other bus...
Let's go!


00:26:33.301 --> 00:26:35.200
Eggshells, carrot-tops...


00:26:35.201 --> 00:26:37.700
- Compost is cool!
Now stuff it in there...


00:26:37.701 --> 00:26:39.100
- Yes sir! Yes sir!
- Very good, very good.


00:26:39.101 --> 00:26:45.100
- Now I'm gonna make a steaming cup of
compost-tea.


00:26:45.101 --> 00:26:46.600
Give me that...


00:26:46.700 --> 00:26:51.746
- Yeah, this is recycling in its most basic form, guys...
- Don't drink it! It's for the plants...


00:26:53.800 --> 00:26:55.000
What's in Jacksonville?


00:26:57.600 --> 00:26:59.000
How did you know about that?


00:27:00.600 --> 00:27:02.300
I... You didn't answer my question.


00:27:03.300 --> 00:27:05.450
Well, you don't answer any of mine, so...


00:27:06.300 --> 00:27:07.800
I mean, you don't even say 'Hi' to me.


00:27:09.100 --> 00:27:10.800
Hi.


00:27:12.200 --> 00:27:14.200
Are you gonna tell me
how you stopped the van?


00:27:14.201 --> 00:27:18.000
Yeah... I had an adrenaline rush.


00:27:18.001 --> 00:27:19.300
It's very common.


00:27:19.301 --> 00:27:21.100
You can Google-it.


00:27:24.700 --> 00:27:25.800
Floridians...


00:27:26.400 --> 00:27:28.100
That's what's in Jacksonville.


00:27:29.500 --> 00:27:31.200
Can you at least watch where you walk?!


00:27:34.900 --> 00:27:37.738
Look... I'm sorry I'm
being rude all the time.


00:27:37.739 --> 00:27:39.300
I just think it's the best way.


00:27:39.301 --> 00:27:41.232
Bella! Guess who's just asked me to Prom.


00:27:44.000 --> 00:27:47.800
- Um, yeah... I actually thought Mike was
gonna ask you...


00:27:49.194 --> 00:27:50.200
Um, it's not gonna be weird though, right?


00:27:50.201 --> 00:27:52.200
No, Zero weirdness.


00:27:52.201 --> 00:27:53.200
You guys are great together.


00:27:53.201 --> 00:27:54.200
I know, right?


00:27:57.100 --> 00:27:58.200
Bella, look.


00:27:58.201 --> 00:28:00.300
It's a worm... It's a worm...


00:28:04.800 --> 00:28:07.400
Bella... We shouldn't be friends.


00:28:10.000 --> 00:28:12.000
- You really should’ve figured that out
a little earlier.


00:28:14.100 --> 00:28:15.900
I mean, why didn't you
just let the van crush me...


00:28:15.901 --> 00:28:17.900
And save yourself all this... regret?


00:28:20.600 --> 00:28:22.200
You think I regret saving you?


00:28:22.201 --> 00:28:23.600
I can see that you do... I just...


00:28:24.900 --> 00:28:25.800
Don't know why.


00:28:26.500 --> 00:28:28.600
You don't know anything.


00:28:29.300 --> 00:28:32.300
- Hi! Um...
Are you gonna be riding with us?


00:28:32.301 --> 00:28:33.600
No, our bus is full.


00:28:44.200 --> 00:28:46.400
Your mom called. Again.


00:28:48.400 --> 00:28:50.949
Well, that's your fault, you shouldn't
have told her about the almost accident.


00:28:50.950 --> 00:28:51.826
Are you finished?


00:28:51.827 --> 00:28:52.900
Yeah.


00:28:54.200 --> 00:28:56.400
- I suppose you're right.
She always did know how to worry.


00:28:59.500 --> 00:29:00.700
She seems different...


00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:03.300
She seems happy.


00:29:07.200 --> 00:29:08.873
Phil sounds like an alright guy...


00:29:11.100 --> 00:29:12.300
Yeah, he is...


00:29:19.600 --> 00:29:20.600
Alright...


00:29:33.100 --> 00:29:35.780
Hey! La Push, baby... Are you in?


00:29:35.782 --> 00:29:37.650
Should I know what that means?


00:29:37.729 --> 00:29:39.800
- La Push Beach down the Quileute Rez.
We're all going tomorrow.


00:29:39.801 --> 00:29:41.165
Yeah, there's a big fun coming in.


00:29:41.166 --> 00:29:43.197
And I don't just surf the Internet.


00:29:43.198 --> 00:29:44.375
Eric, you stood up once...


00:29:44.376 --> 00:29:45.591
And it was a foam board.


00:29:45.592 --> 00:29:47.753
- But there's whale watching too.
Come with us.


00:29:47.754 --> 00:29:48.903
La Push, baby...


00:29:48.904 --> 00:29:50.932
It's... La Push.


00:29:51.400 --> 00:29:53.100
I'll go if you stop saying that, okay?


00:29:53.400 --> 00:29:55.014
Seriously dude... It's creepy, man.


00:29:56.400 --> 00:29:57.363
Edible art?


00:30:01.293 --> 00:30:02.099
Bella.


00:30:03.612 --> 00:30:04.500
Thanks.


00:30:05.288 --> 00:30:07.413
- You know, your mood swings are kind of
giving me a whiplash.


00:30:10.770 --> 00:30:13.629
I only said it'd be better for you if we
weren't friends, not that I didn't want to be.


00:30:13.678 --> 00:30:14.571
What does that mean?


00:30:16.104 --> 00:30:19.245
It means, if you're smart,
you'd stay away from me.


00:30:20.582 --> 00:30:22.869
- Well, let's say for argument sake that
I'm not smart.


00:30:23.866 --> 00:30:24.712
Will you tell me truth?


00:30:24.904 --> 00:30:26.218
No, probably not.


00:30:27.992 --> 00:30:29.228
I'd rather hear your theories.


00:30:31.821 --> 00:30:37.579
- I have considered... Radioactive spiders
and Kryptonite.


00:30:39.000 --> 00:30:40.841
That's all super-hero stuff, right?


00:30:41.794 --> 00:30:43.020
What if I'm not the hero?


00:30:43.021 --> 00:30:44.216
What if I'm...


00:30:44.289 --> 00:30:45.465
The bad guy?


00:30:45.466 --> 00:30:47.203
You're not.


00:30:48.496 --> 00:30:50.435
I can see what you're trying to put off.


00:30:50.516 --> 00:30:52.770
But I can see that it's just
to keep people away from you.


00:30:52.771 --> 00:30:53.642
That's a mask.


00:30:58.453 --> 00:31:00.061
Why don't we just...


00:31:01.284 --> 00:31:02.296
Hang out?


00:31:04.282 --> 00:31:05.800
Everybody is going to the beach.


00:31:05.801 --> 00:31:06.894
Come...


00:31:08.600 --> 00:31:12.085
I mean, have fun.


00:31:14.690 --> 00:31:15.938
Which beach?


00:31:15.939 --> 00:31:16.939
La Push.


00:31:17.959 --> 00:31:19.500
I don’t know...


00:31:21.571 --> 00:31:23.260
Is there something wrong with that beach?


00:31:27.153 --> 00:31:28.534
It's just a little crowded.


00:31:34.237 --> 00:31:35.200
Its freezing...


00:31:35.201 --> 00:31:36.421
You gotta go out, folks...


00:31:37.966 --> 00:31:39.366
I don't know if it's worth it anymore.


00:31:39.367 --> 00:31:42.036
We're all the way out here...


00:31:42.715 --> 00:31:44.000
You guys are babies.


00:31:44.001 --> 00:31:46.553
- So, I keep thinking that Eric's gonna
ask me to the Prom...


00:31:47.910 --> 00:31:50.197
And he just... doesn't.


00:31:52.700 --> 00:31:54.065
You should ask him.


00:31:55.759 --> 00:31:58.783
Take control. You’re a
strong independent woman.


00:31:59.486 --> 00:32:00.486
I am?


00:32:00.487 --> 00:32:01.487
Yes.


00:32:02.753 --> 00:32:03.753
Can you help me out?


00:32:03.754 --> 00:32:04.754
Yeah.


00:32:06.659 --> 00:32:07.659
Bella!


00:32:07.660 --> 00:32:10.098
- Hi Jacob!
Guys, this is Jacob.


00:32:10.099 --> 00:32:11.085
Hey, Guys. How you doing?


00:32:11.120 --> 00:32:13.100
- Hi.
- Hey.


00:32:14.065 --> 00:32:15.476
What are you, like, stalking me?


00:32:16.059 --> 00:32:17.330
You're on my rez, remember?


00:32:18.767 --> 00:32:19.726
Are you surfing?


00:32:20.744 --> 00:32:21.744
Definitely not.


00:32:22.894 --> 00:32:25.581
- You guys should keep Bella company.
Um, her date bailed.


00:32:25.582 --> 00:32:26.582
What date?


00:32:26.583 --> 00:32:28.448
She invited Edward.


00:32:28.449 --> 00:32:30.077
To be polite, that's it.


00:32:30.078 --> 00:32:32.500
- I think it's nice she invited him.
Nobody ever does.


00:32:32.501 --> 00:32:33.501
Yeah, 'cause Cullen's a freak.


00:32:33.502 --> 00:32:35.300
You got that right!


00:32:36.493 --> 00:32:37.493
You guys know him?


00:32:38.187 --> 00:32:39.537
The Cullens don't come here.


00:32:48.556 --> 00:32:50.166
What did your friends mean about...


00:32:50.167 --> 00:32:52.800
You know, 'The Cullens don't come here'?


00:32:53.449 --> 00:32:54.650
You caught that, huh?


00:32:56.780 --> 00:32:59.700
I'm not really supposed
to say anything about it.


00:33:01.014 --> 00:33:02.500
Hey, I can keep a secret.


00:33:03.709 --> 00:33:08.100
Um, really it's just
like an old scary story...


00:33:10.243 --> 00:33:11.963
Well, I want to know.


00:33:15.251 --> 00:33:19.640
- Okay, did you know that Quileutes
are supposedly descendants from wolves?


00:33:20.396 --> 00:33:21.396
What?


00:33:21.500 --> 00:33:24.100
Like wolves... Real wolves?


00:33:26.274 --> 00:33:28.135
Yeah... That's a legend of our tribe.


00:33:28.564 --> 00:33:31.206
Okay... So, what's the
story about the Cullens?


00:33:33.808 --> 00:33:36.464
- Well, they're supposedly descendants from
this, like...


00:33:36.877 --> 00:33:38.252
Enemy clan.


00:33:41.494 --> 00:33:45.043
- My great-grandfather, the chief,
found them hunting on our land.


00:33:46.577 --> 00:33:51.004
But they claimed to be something
different, so... We made a treaty with them.


00:33:51.332 --> 00:33:53.677
If they promised to say off Quileute lands,


00:33:53.678 --> 00:33:56.299
then we wouldn't expose
what they really were to...


00:33:56.300 --> 00:33:58.451
The pale faces.


00:33:59.679 --> 00:34:01.094
I thought they just moved here...


00:34:02.762 --> 00:34:04.302
Or just moved back.


00:34:12.424 --> 00:34:14.005
What are they really?


00:34:14.006 --> 00:34:15.854
It's just a story, Bella.


00:34:17.685 --> 00:34:18.708
Come on, let's go.


00:34:42.444 --> 00:34:43.472
Hello?


00:34:50.834 --> 00:34:51.712
Girl?


00:34:53.231 --> 00:34:54.400
Girl!


00:35:14.116 --> 00:35:15.109
Hello.


00:35:16.363 --> 00:35:17.714
Nice jacket.


00:35:21.043 --> 00:35:21.842
Who are you?


00:35:22.043 --> 00:35:24.107
It's always the same inane questions...


00:35:24.921 --> 00:35:26.218
'Who are you?'


00:35:26.219 --> 00:35:27.564
'What do you want?'


00:35:28.531 --> 00:35:30.550
'Why are you doing this?'


00:35:30.551 --> 00:35:32.051
James...


00:35:32.817 --> 00:35:34.906
Let's not play with our food.


00:36:23.711 --> 00:36:24.873
He's not here.


00:36:27.481 --> 00:36:29.727
Whenever the weather's
nice the Cullens disappear.


00:36:31.486 --> 00:36:32.693
What? They just ditch?


00:36:33.062 --> 00:36:37.807
- No, Dr. and Mrs. Cullen yank them out for
hiking and camping and stuff.


00:36:37.808 --> 00:36:40.195
- I tried that on my parents...
Not even close.


00:36:40.196 --> 00:36:42.939
Guys! I'm going to the Prom with Eric.


00:36:42.940 --> 00:36:45.117
I just asked him... I took control.


00:36:45.118 --> 00:36:46.615
I told you that would happen.


00:36:46.616 --> 00:36:48.716
Are you sure you have to go out of town?


00:36:49.317 --> 00:36:51.539
Oh, yeah. It's a weird family thing.


00:36:51.979 --> 00:36:55.522
Okay, we should go shopping to Port Angeles
before all the good dresses get cleaned out.


00:36:59.043 --> 00:37:00.140
Port Angeles?


00:37:01.060 --> 00:37:01.907
You mind if I come?


00:37:02.117 --> 00:37:03.777
Yeah! I need your opinion...


00:37:06.026 --> 00:37:07.154
I like this one...


00:37:07.155 --> 00:37:08.155
That's cool.


00:37:08.156 --> 00:37:10.138
But I don't know about
the one-shoulder thing...


00:37:10.139 --> 00:37:10.968
I like this one.


00:37:10.969 --> 00:37:12.764
Yeah, I like the knitting.


00:37:12.765 --> 00:37:14.122
Jess, what do you think? Lavender?


00:37:14.123 --> 00:37:15.371
Is that good? Is that my color?


00:37:15.372 --> 00:37:18.124
I like it. I like that dusty-rose one too.


00:37:18.125 --> 00:37:20.617
- Okay, I like this one...
It makes my boobs look good.


00:37:20.900 --> 00:37:23.000
Hey! Nice!


00:37:25.446 --> 00:37:27.106
That is uncomfortable.


00:37:27.107 --> 00:37:28.152
Oh, it's disgusting...


00:37:29.175 --> 00:37:30.260
Bella, what do you think?


00:37:32.663 --> 00:37:33.802
Looks great.


00:37:34.715 --> 00:37:36.461
You said that about the
last five dresses though.


00:37:37.824 --> 00:37:39.281
I thought they were pretty good.


00:37:39.282 --> 00:37:41.696
Not really into this, are you?


00:37:42.636 --> 00:37:44.437
- I, actually, really just wanna go
to this bookstore...


00:37:46.197 --> 00:37:47.633
Meet you guys at the restaurant?


00:37:47.998 --> 00:37:48.895
Are you sure?


00:37:48.896 --> 00:37:50.483
Yeah, see you in a minute.


00:37:50.484 --> 00:37:52.000
- Okay.
- Okay.


00:37:54.037 --> 00:37:55.764
She's right though... It looks awesome.


00:37:59.099 --> 00:38:00.025
Here you go...


00:38:02.000 --> 00:38:03.539
Good night.


00:38:03.712 --> 00:38:04.541
Thank you.


00:38:36.810 --> 00:38:37.989
We saw you at the dress shop.


00:38:37.990 --> 00:38:40.275
Hey, where are you running to?


00:38:40.276 --> 00:38:42.206
There she is...


00:38:43.298 --> 00:38:44.839
How are you guys doing?


00:38:44.840 --> 00:38:45.986
What's up, girl?


00:38:45.987 --> 00:38:48.109
Whoa! Where are you going?


00:38:48.110 --> 00:38:49.244
Where are you going?


00:38:49.649 --> 00:38:52.020
Hang out with us.


00:38:52.669 --> 00:38:55.000
What's the problem?


00:38:55.001 --> 00:38:56.350
- You're pretty.
- Don't touch me.


00:38:56.351 --> 00:38:57.911
Seriously, you should...


00:38:57.946 --> 00:38:59.185
Don't touch me!


00:39:07.463 --> 00:39:08.718
Get in the car.


00:39:10.973 --> 00:39:13.900
That was a very dangerous... move.


00:39:40.218 --> 00:39:42.250
- I should go back there and rip
those guy's heads off.


00:39:42.251 --> 00:39:44.023
No, you shouldn't.


00:39:44.024 --> 00:39:46.562
- You don't know the vile, repulsive things
they're thinking.


00:39:46.926 --> 00:39:47.860
And you do?


00:39:49.276 --> 00:39:50.591
It was not hard to guess.


00:39:52.361 --> 00:39:53.584
Can you talk about something else...


00:39:53.585 --> 00:39:55.272
And distract me so I won't turn around?


00:39:57.963 --> 00:39:59.434
Can you just put your seatbelt on?


00:40:01.485 --> 00:40:03.448
Put your own seatbelt on.


00:40:10.547 --> 00:40:11.476
Hey! Guys, I'm sorry. I just...


00:40:11.477 --> 00:40:13.531
Where were you? We left you messages.


00:40:13.532 --> 00:40:16.206
We waited but we were starving, so we...


00:40:17.793 --> 00:40:20.058
I'm sorry I kept Bella from dinner.


00:40:20.059 --> 00:40:22.725
We just ran into each other and got talking.


00:40:25.932 --> 00:40:28.429
No, we totally understand, I mean...


00:40:28.430 --> 00:40:30.045
That happens, right?


00:40:31.662 --> 00:40:33.605
Um, we were just leaving so...


00:40:35.242 --> 00:40:36.049
Bella, you wanna...


00:40:37.197 --> 00:40:39.682
- I think I should make sure Bella
gets something to eat...


00:40:40.611 --> 00:40:41.630
If you'd like.


00:40:43.756 --> 00:40:45.064
I'll drive you home myself.


00:40:45.065 --> 00:40:48.092
That's so... thoughtful.


00:40:48.093 --> 00:40:50.392
It's really thoughtful, yeah.


00:40:51.420 --> 00:40:53.814
Yeah, I should eat something.


00:40:55.904 --> 00:40:59.160
Okay, so... I'll see you tomorrow.


00:40:59.170 --> 00:41:00.360
- See you...
- Okay.


00:41:12.098 --> 00:41:13.507
One Mushroom Ravioli.


00:41:14.223 --> 00:41:15.123
Thanks.


00:41:15.124 --> 00:41:17.095
Yeah, no problem.


00:41:17.464 --> 00:41:20.037
So... Are you sure there isn't
anything I can get for you?


00:41:20.038 --> 00:41:21.129
No, no. Thank you.


00:41:22.289 --> 00:41:23.565
Let me know...


00:41:29.960 --> 00:41:31.512
You're really not gonna eat?


00:41:34.535 --> 00:41:37.828
No, I'm on a... special diet.


00:41:39.296 --> 00:41:40.903
You gotta give me some answers.


00:41:43.063 --> 00:41:44.104
Yes... No...


00:41:45.122 --> 00:41:47.186
To get to the other side...


00:41:48.357 --> 00:41:50.196
1,77245...


00:41:50.197 --> 00:41:52.088
I don't want to know what
the square root of Pi is.


00:41:52.708 --> 00:41:53.509
You knew that?


00:41:54.090 --> 00:41:56.314
How did you know where I was?


00:41:56.655 --> 00:41:57.479
I didn't.


00:41:58.322 --> 00:41:59.155
Alright...


00:42:01.072 --> 00:42:02.478
Don't leave...


00:42:06.617 --> 00:42:08.796
Did you... follow me?


00:42:11.534 --> 00:42:16.651
I feel very... protective of you.


00:42:19.283 --> 00:42:20.519
So you followed me.


00:42:20.520 --> 00:42:23.667
- I was trying to keep a distance unless
you needed my help and then...


00:42:23.668 --> 00:42:27.621
I heard what those
low-lives were thinking...


00:42:27.622 --> 00:42:28.652
Wait...


00:42:29.584 --> 00:42:31.715
You say you heard what they were thinking?


00:42:35.500 --> 00:42:39.936
So what... You read minds...


00:42:42.936 --> 00:42:46.809
I can read every mind in this room...


00:42:47.780 --> 00:42:49.197
Apart from yours.


00:42:52.765 --> 00:42:55.903
- Money...
Sex...


00:42:57.200 --> 00:43:00.143
- Money...
Sex...


00:43:00.244 --> 00:43:01.376
Cat.


00:43:04.645 --> 00:43:07.881
And then you... Nothing.


00:43:09.416 --> 00:43:11.243
It's very frustrating.


00:43:14.119 --> 00:43:15.532
There's something wrong with me?


00:43:17.843 --> 00:43:22.232
- I tell you I can read minds and you
think there's something wrong with you.


00:43:30.800 --> 00:43:31.629
What is it?


00:43:32.869 --> 00:43:34.396
I don't have...


00:43:34.397 --> 00:43:36.597
The strength...


00:43:37.881 --> 00:43:40.104
To stay away from you anymore.


00:43:41.505 --> 00:43:43.956
Then don't.


00:44:04.123 --> 00:44:05.123
Okay, I think I'm warm enough now.


00:44:12.428 --> 00:44:14.140
Your hand is so cold.


00:44:25.305 --> 00:44:27.865
Whoa! What is going on?


00:44:30.039 --> 00:44:32.932
- My dad's still here.
Can you pull in?


00:44:36.447 --> 00:44:38.032
It's my father's car in there.


00:44:39.055 --> 00:44:40.534
What is he doing here?


00:44:43.768 --> 00:44:45.208
Carlisle, what's going on?


00:44:47.555 --> 00:44:50.660
Waylon Forge was found in
a boat out near his place.


00:44:51.791 --> 00:44:52.937
I just examined the body.


00:44:53.643 --> 00:44:54.570
He died?


00:44:56.049 --> 00:44:56.992
How?


00:44:57.278 --> 00:44:58.488
Animal attack.


00:45:00.773 --> 00:45:03.289
- Was it the same one that got that
security guard down at Mason?


00:45:03.788 --> 00:45:04.900
Most likely.


00:45:05.375 --> 00:45:06.657
It must be getting closer to town then...


00:45:06.658 --> 00:45:07.420
Bella,


00:45:07.430 --> 00:45:08.698
you should go inside.


00:45:09.022 --> 00:45:10.720
Waylon was your father's friend.


00:45:11.746 --> 00:45:12.700
Okay...


00:45:16.612 --> 00:45:17.754
Um, I'll see you later.


00:45:30.800 --> 00:45:31.600
Hey...


00:45:36.100 --> 00:45:37.830
Dad, I'm really sorry.


00:45:42.655 --> 00:45:44.791
Not one gone in thirty years.


00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:03.029
Don't worry, we're gonna find this thing.


00:46:04.521 --> 00:46:05.665
In the meantime,


00:46:07.244 --> 00:46:09.215
I want you to carry this with you.


00:46:11.900 --> 00:46:14.659
- I don't know if...
- It would give your old man some peace of mind.


00:46:20.660 --> 00:46:21.666
Let's go home.


00:49:16.166 --> 00:49:18.041
You're impossibly fast...


00:49:18.076 --> 00:49:19.318
And strong.


00:49:20.585 --> 00:49:23.532
Your skin is pale white and ice cold.


00:49:24.366 --> 00:49:25.896
Your eyes change color...


00:49:27.222 --> 00:49:28.809
And sometimes you speak like...


00:49:29.503 --> 00:49:31.756
Like you're from a different time.


00:49:33.097 --> 00:49:34.766
You never eat or drink anything...


00:49:34.828 --> 00:49:36.203
You don't go out in the sunlight.


00:49:40.637 --> 00:49:41.755
How old are you?


00:49:43.616 --> 00:49:44.529
Seventeen.


00:49:46.993 --> 00:49:48.858
How long have you been seventeen?


00:49:52.667 --> 00:49:53.988
A while.


00:50:07.215 --> 00:50:08.459
I know what you are.


00:50:11.699 --> 00:50:12.584
Say it...


00:50:16.674 --> 00:50:17.700
Out loud.


00:50:20.885 --> 00:50:21.916
Say it!


00:50:28.065 --> 00:50:29.256
Vampire.


00:50:32.586 --> 00:50:34.277
Are you afraid?


00:50:42.509 --> 00:50:43.729
No.


00:50:46.246 --> 00:50:48.653
Then ask me the most basic question:


00:50:49.530 --> 00:50:51.094
'What do we eat?'


00:50:54.103 --> 00:50:55.344
You won't hurt me.


00:51:00.417 --> 00:51:01.654
Where are we going?


00:51:03.566 --> 00:51:06.405
Up the mountain, out of the cloud bag.


00:51:07.042 --> 00:51:09.231
You need to see what I
look like in the sunlight.


00:51:28.888 --> 00:51:31.334
This is why we don't show
ourselves in sunlight.


00:51:31.706 --> 00:51:33.504
People would know we're different.


00:51:44.630 --> 00:51:45.827
This is what I am.


00:51:51.552 --> 00:51:52.994
It's like diamonds...


00:52:02.786 --> 00:52:03.786
You're beautiful.


00:52:07.120 --> 00:52:10.824
- Beautiful...?
This is the skin of a killer, Bella.


00:52:17.788 --> 00:52:19.456
I'm a killer.


00:52:21.382 --> 00:52:22.862
I don't believe that.


00:52:23.965 --> 00:52:26.122
That's because you believe the lie...


00:52:27.395 --> 00:52:28.968
The camouflage.


00:52:31.788 --> 00:52:34.074
I'm the world's most dangerous predator.


00:52:34.877 --> 00:52:38.468
Everything about me invites you in...


00:52:38.469 --> 00:52:42.469
My voice, my face... Even my smell.


00:52:42.832 --> 00:52:45.175
As if I would need any of that.


00:52:48.375 --> 00:52:50.037
As if you could outrun me!


00:52:56.084 --> 00:52:58.078
As if you could fight me off.


00:53:01.932 --> 00:53:03.594
I'm designed to kill.


00:53:06.793 --> 00:53:08.205
I don't care.


00:53:09.285 --> 00:53:11.364
I've killed people before.


00:53:12.833 --> 00:53:14.838
It doesn't matter.


00:53:19.713 --> 00:53:21.364
I wanted to kill you.


00:53:24.933 --> 00:53:29.850
- I've never wanted a human's blood
so much in my life.


00:53:30.692 --> 00:53:32.043
I trust you.


00:53:34.644 --> 00:53:36.062
Don't.


00:53:37.405 --> 00:53:38.878
I'm here, I trust you.


00:53:43.814 --> 00:53:46.656
- My family, we're different from
others of our kind.


00:53:46.657 --> 00:53:48.559
We only hunt animals...


00:53:48.560 --> 00:53:50.871
We've learned to control our thirst.


00:53:54.100 --> 00:53:59.517
- As to you... Your scent...
Is like a drug to me.


00:54:01.113 --> 00:54:05.473
Like my own personal brand of heroin.


00:54:11.815 --> 00:54:14.308
Then, why did you hate
me so much when we met?


00:54:14.833 --> 00:54:19.447
I did. Only for making me want you so badly.


00:54:20.441 --> 00:54:22.645
I still don't know if I can control myself.


00:54:24.712 --> 00:54:26.715
I know you can.


00:54:35.028 --> 00:54:37.098
I can't read your mind,


00:54:37.628 --> 00:54:40.457
you have to tell me what you're thinking.


00:54:43.424 --> 00:54:44.896
Now I'm afraid.


00:54:50.274 --> 00:54:51.111
Good.


00:54:52.213 --> 00:54:54.367
I'm not afraid of you...


00:54:57.913 --> 00:54:59.891
I'm only afraid of losing you...


00:54:59.892 --> 00:55:01.605
Like you're going to disappear.


00:55:09.421 --> 00:55:12.100
You don't know how long I've waited for you.


00:55:20.983 --> 00:55:23.375
And so the lion fell
in love with the lamb...


00:55:27.605 --> 00:55:28.687
What a stupid lamb.


00:55:28.688 --> 00:55:31.924
What a sick, masochistic lion.


00:56:57.144 --> 00:56:59.878
About three things I
was absolutely positive:


00:57:01.512 --> 00:57:06.017
First, Edward was a vampire.


00:57:10.389 --> 00:57:13.936
Second, there was a part of him,


00:57:14.729 --> 00:57:17.024
and I didn't know how
dominant that part might be,


00:57:18.469 --> 00:57:20.242
that thirsted for my blood.


00:57:24.367 --> 00:57:25.597
And third,


00:57:26.820 --> 00:57:31.070
I was unconditionally and
irrevocably in love with him.


00:57:36.413 --> 00:57:39.044
Monte Carlo? That's our Prom theme?


00:57:39.045 --> 00:57:43.013
Uhu, gambling... Tuxedos...


00:57:43.014 --> 00:57:44.395
And Bond... James Bond.


00:57:48.100 --> 00:57:50.530
Oh... My... God...


00:58:02.244 --> 00:58:04.162
You know, everybody's staring...


00:58:08.731 --> 00:58:10.487
Not that guy...


00:58:10.841 --> 00:58:12.421
No, he just looked.


00:58:14.600 --> 00:58:16.428
I'm breaking all the rules now anyway...


00:58:17.291 --> 00:58:19.218
Since I'm going to hell.


00:58:23.963 --> 00:58:26.600
So... Does a person have to be dying...


00:58:29.337 --> 00:58:30.523
To become like you?


00:58:31.704 --> 00:58:34.765
No, that's just Carlisle.


00:58:36.450 --> 00:58:38.705
- He'd never do this to someone
who had another choice.


00:58:41.092 --> 00:58:43.198
So, how long have you been like this?


00:58:45.021 --> 00:58:46.455
Since 1918...


00:58:47.488 --> 00:58:49.029
That's when Carlisle found me...


00:58:49.030 --> 00:58:50.823
Dying of Spanish Influenza.


00:58:52.964 --> 00:58:54.359
What was it like?


00:58:55.288 --> 00:58:58.023
The venom was excruciating...


00:58:58.527 --> 00:59:00.590
But what Carlisle did was much harder.


00:59:00.894 --> 00:59:02.993
- Not many of us have the restraint
to do that.


00:59:03.060 --> 00:59:05.852
But didn't he just have to... bite?


00:59:08.049 --> 00:59:09.761
Not exactly.


00:59:10.218 --> 00:59:12.818
When we taste...


00:59:14.238 --> 00:59:15.441
Human blood...


00:59:15.442 --> 00:59:17.858
A sort of frenzy begins.


00:59:19.279 --> 00:59:22.245
It's almost impossible to stop.


00:59:23.374 --> 00:59:25.449
But Carlisle did.


00:59:25.450 --> 00:59:26.836
First with me...


00:59:26.837 --> 00:59:28.307
And then with his wife, Esme.


00:59:28.342 --> 00:59:33.250
- So, is Carlisle the real reason that
you don't... kill people?


00:59:36.564 --> 00:59:38.494
No, that's not the only reason...


00:59:41.450 --> 00:59:44.564
I don't want to be a monster.


00:59:46.029 --> 00:59:49.389
My family, we think of
ourselves as vegetarians...


00:59:49.390 --> 00:59:52.400
'Cause we only survive
on the blood of animals.


00:59:53.349 --> 00:59:58.260
It's like a human only living on toffee.


00:59:58.261 --> 01:00:03.413
It keeps you strong but
you're never fully satisfied.


01:00:06.132 --> 01:00:08.808
It wouldn't be like drinking
your blood, for instance...


01:00:15.008 --> 01:00:17.409
Was it other vampires that killed Waylon?


01:00:18.354 --> 01:00:19.340
Yeah,


01:00:19.351 --> 01:00:20.621
there are others out there...


01:00:20.622 --> 01:00:23.636
We run into them from time to time.


01:00:25.559 --> 01:00:29.367
- Can the rest of your family read
people's minds like you can?


01:00:32.187 --> 01:00:34.667
No, no. That's just me.


01:00:34.848 --> 01:00:38.329
But Alice can see the future.


01:00:38.960 --> 01:00:41.427
I bet she saw me coming.


01:00:42.610 --> 01:00:44.831
Alice's vision is subjective...


01:00:45.166 --> 01:00:47.796
I mean, the future can always change.


01:00:58.934 --> 01:01:00.390
Can you act human?


01:01:00.412 --> 01:01:01.547
I mean, I've got neighbors.


01:01:01.548 --> 01:01:03.193
I'm gonna take you to my place tomorrow.


01:01:05.718 --> 01:01:06.635
Thanks...


01:01:07.767 --> 01:01:09.068
Wait, with your family?


01:01:09.998 --> 01:01:11.362
Yeah.


01:01:12.048 --> 01:01:13.283
What if they don't like me?


01:01:14.990 --> 01:01:18.609
So you're worried... Not because you'll
be in a house full of vampires but...


01:01:18.610 --> 01:01:21.806
Because you think they won't approve of you?


01:01:21.807 --> 01:01:23.300
I'm glad I missed you.


01:01:25.312 --> 01:01:26.361
What is it?


01:01:28.261 --> 01:01:29.686
A complication.


01:01:31.993 --> 01:01:33.032
I'll pick you up tomorrow.


01:02:00.000 --> 01:02:03.097
Hey! Come to visit your truck?


01:02:03.098 --> 01:02:04.848
Looks good...


01:02:05.440 --> 01:02:06.671
- Got that dent out...
- Yeah.


01:02:06.749 --> 01:02:08.873
Actually, we came to visit your flat-screen.


01:02:08.874 --> 01:02:10.718
First Mariners game of the season.


01:02:11.304 --> 01:02:14.224
- Plus, Jacob here keeps bugging me
about seeing you again.


01:02:14.959 --> 01:02:16.945
Great, dad... Thanks.


01:02:16.946 --> 01:02:18.719
Just keeping it real, son.


01:02:20.959 --> 01:02:21.788
Pale Ale.


01:02:21.789 --> 01:02:23.743
Well done, Chief...


01:02:24.264 --> 01:02:27.014
Harry Clearwater's homemade fish fry.


01:02:27.015 --> 01:02:27.836
Good.


01:02:30.747 --> 01:02:32.839
Any luck with that Waylon case?


01:02:32.840 --> 01:02:34.911
Well, I don't think it was
an animal that killed him.


01:02:35.415 --> 01:02:36.991
I never thought it was...


01:02:38.705 --> 01:02:40.871
You spread the word out at the rez, huh?


01:02:40.872 --> 01:02:42.226
Keep the kids out of the woods...


01:02:42.423 --> 01:02:43.515
Will do.


01:02:44.503 --> 01:02:46.533
Don't want no one else getting hurt, do we?


01:03:21.300 --> 01:03:22.582
This is incredible.


01:03:26.256 --> 01:03:28.600
It's so white and open, you know.


01:03:30.560 --> 01:03:31.869
What did you expect...


01:03:32.612 --> 01:03:34.430
Coffins and dungeons and moats?


01:03:34.961 --> 01:03:37.288
No, not the moats.


01:03:38.387 --> 01:03:39.429
Not the moats...


01:03:46.900 --> 01:03:49.042
This is the one place we don't have to hide.


01:03:52.503 --> 01:03:53.720
I told them not to do this.


01:04:05.281 --> 01:04:06.907
Is she even Italian?


01:04:06.942 --> 01:04:08.500
Her name is Bella.


01:04:08.501 --> 01:04:09.809
I'm sure she'll love it no matter what.


01:04:09.844 --> 01:04:13.288
Get a whiff of that...


01:04:13.830 --> 01:04:15.740
Here comes the human...


01:04:19.720 --> 01:04:22.352
Bella! We're making Italiano for you.


01:04:23.836 --> 01:04:27.959
- Bella, this is Esme. My mother
for all intents and purposes.


01:04:28.200 --> 01:04:29.063
Bon giorno.


01:04:29.100 --> 01:04:29.904
Molto Bene!


01:04:30.793 --> 01:04:33.284
- You've given us an excuse to use
the kitchen for the first time.


01:04:33.285 --> 01:04:34.187
I hope you're hungry.


01:04:34.466 --> 01:04:35.637
Yeah, absolutely...


01:04:35.672 --> 01:04:36.626
She already ate.


01:04:43.189 --> 01:04:44.022
Perfect!


01:04:45.185 --> 01:04:47.885
Yeah, it's just...


01:04:47.920 --> 01:04:49.246
I know you guys don't eat...


01:04:49.281 --> 01:04:52.268
Of course, it's very considerate of you.


01:04:52.303 --> 01:04:53.965
Just ignore Rosalie. I do.


01:04:54.465 --> 01:04:57.569
- Yeah, let's just keep pretending
like this isn't dangerous for all of us.


01:04:57.604 --> 01:05:01.320
I would never tell anybody anything...


01:05:01.355 --> 01:05:03.068
She knows that.


01:05:03.103 --> 01:05:05.453
Yeah, well, the problem is...


01:05:05.488 --> 01:05:07.603
You two have become public now, so...


01:05:07.809 --> 01:05:09.148
- Emmett!
- No, she should know.


01:05:09.721 --> 01:05:12.931
The entire family will be
implicated if this ends badly.


01:05:13.480 --> 01:05:15.512
Badly as in...


01:05:17.306 --> 01:05:19.682
I become the meal.


01:05:27.007 --> 01:05:28.019
Hi, Bella!


01:05:32.186 --> 01:05:33.525
I'm Alice.


01:05:35.100 --> 01:05:36.200
Hi.


01:05:37.243 --> 01:05:39.136
Oh, you do smell good.


01:05:39.171 --> 01:05:41.403
Alice, what are you...?


01:05:41.438 --> 01:05:43.890
It's ok. Bella and I are
gonna be great friends.


01:05:48.158 --> 01:05:50.277
Sorry, Jasper's our newest vegetarian.


01:05:50.312 --> 01:05:51.915
It's a little difficult for him.


01:05:52.394 --> 01:05:53.968
It's a pleasure to meet you.


01:05:54.003 --> 01:05:57.518
It's okay, Jasper. You won't hurt her.


01:05:57.962 --> 01:05:59.551
Alright...


01:05:59.586 --> 01:06:01.826
I'm gonna take you on a tour
of the rest of the house.


01:06:03.258 --> 01:06:04.684
I'll see you soon...


01:06:04.719 --> 01:06:05.549
Okay.


01:06:08.800 --> 01:06:10.186
Cute...


01:06:10.187 --> 01:06:11.410
I think that went well.


01:06:11.445 --> 01:06:12.604
Clean this up.


01:06:13.432 --> 01:06:14.311
Now!


01:06:24.757 --> 01:06:26.173
Graduation caps?


01:06:27.333 --> 01:06:28.234
Yeah,


01:06:28.269 --> 01:06:30.679
it's a private joke.


01:06:30.714 --> 01:06:32.745
We matriculate a lot.


01:06:34.692 --> 01:06:38.873
That's kind of miserable. I mean,
repeating High School over and over...


01:06:38.908 --> 01:06:42.005
- Sure but the younger we start out in
a new place,


01:06:42.040 --> 01:06:42.991
the longer we can stay there.


01:06:43.556 --> 01:06:44.697
Come on...


01:06:55.706 --> 01:06:57.188
Um, yeah... This is my room.


01:07:10.166 --> 01:07:11.467
No bed?


01:07:11.502 --> 01:07:13.564
No,


01:07:14.736 --> 01:07:15.862
I don't sleep.


01:07:16.766 --> 01:07:17.834
Ever?


01:07:17.869 --> 01:07:19.517
No.


01:07:22.500 --> 01:07:23.420
Okay...


01:07:32.432 --> 01:07:34.768
You have so much music.


01:07:34.803 --> 01:07:36.626
What were you listening to?


01:07:40.297 --> 01:07:42.627
It's Debussy.


01:07:45.500 --> 01:07:46.627
Yeah.


01:07:51.027 --> 01:07:52.548
Clair de Lune is great.


01:08:27.446 --> 01:08:28.726
What?


01:08:29.501 --> 01:08:30.543
I can't dance.


01:08:39.500 --> 01:08:41.380
Well, I can always make you.


01:08:44.152 --> 01:08:45.629
I'm not scared of you.


01:08:48.331 --> 01:08:51.415
Well, you really shouldn't have said that.


01:08:56.451 --> 01:08:59.158
You better hold on tight, spider monkey.


01:09:04.943 --> 01:09:06.221
Do you trust me?


01:09:06.694 --> 01:09:08.587
In theory.


01:09:09.369 --> 01:09:10.508
Then close your eyes.


01:09:35.727 --> 01:09:36.988
What?


01:09:37.426 --> 01:09:39.812
This isn't real.


01:09:39.847 --> 01:09:42.388
This kind of stuff just doesn't exist.


01:09:42.423 --> 01:09:44.670
It does in my world.


01:11:14.900 --> 01:11:16.300
Whoa! Hold on.


01:11:21.635 --> 01:11:22.659
It's human.


01:11:27.149 --> 01:11:32.898
- Arizona! Yo, what's happening?
So... You and Cullen, huh?


01:11:32.899 --> 01:11:33.724
That's...


01:11:33.725 --> 01:11:35.373
I don't like it,


01:11:36.399 --> 01:11:40.004
- I mean... He looks at you like
you're something to eat.


01:11:43.767 --> 01:11:44.962
Here's your veggie plate...


01:11:46.949 --> 01:11:49.671
I'm sorry I'm late. Biology Projects.


01:11:50.408 --> 01:11:51.838
I ordered you the Spam Salad.


01:11:51.839 --> 01:11:52.869
I hope that's okay.


01:11:53.275 --> 01:11:55.072
You should order one for yourself next time.


01:11:55.488 --> 01:11:56.669
Cup-egg on a steak...


01:11:57.695 --> 01:11:59.901
Hey, I'm as healthy as a horse.


01:12:00.601 --> 01:12:03.320
So, Chief... Boys wanna know,


01:12:04.727 --> 01:12:07.202
- Did you find anything down by
Creek Silver today?


01:12:11.006 --> 01:12:12.948
Yeah, We found a bare human footprint.


01:12:12.981 --> 01:12:15.800
- But it looks like whatever that is,
it's headed to east.


01:12:15.801 --> 01:12:18.401
- So, Ketsap's County sheriff is gonna
take over from here.


01:12:18.600 --> 01:12:19.580
Okay...


01:12:19.592 --> 01:12:20.498
Okay?


01:12:20.617 --> 01:12:22.495
I just hope they catch them fast.


01:12:32.202 --> 01:12:33.819
Looks like your friends are flagging you.


01:12:36.778 --> 01:12:38.780
It's okay. If you wanna go, join them.


01:12:38.781 --> 01:12:40.308
I was gonna try to leave early anyway.


01:12:41.218 --> 01:12:42.485
Me too.


01:12:42.784 --> 01:12:45.052
Bella, Friday night... Go out.


01:12:46.281 --> 01:12:48.932
- Looks like the Newton boy's got
a big smile for you.


01:12:48.933 --> 01:12:50.208
Yeah, he's a good buddy.


01:12:51.766 --> 01:12:53.880
Better than any of these
other yahoos in town.


01:12:54.300 --> 01:12:55.410
Anybody you're interested?


01:12:57.492 --> 01:12:59.071
Dad, we're gonna talk about boys?


01:13:01.282 --> 01:13:02.440
I guess not.


01:13:03.828 --> 01:13:07.207
I just feel like I leave alone too much...


01:13:07.208 --> 01:13:09.483
You should be around people.


01:13:10.377 --> 01:13:12.254
I don't mind being alone...


01:13:13.611 --> 01:13:16.227
I guess I'm kind of like my dad in that way.


01:13:21.200 --> 01:13:23.634
So, how's all the baseball stuff going?


01:13:23.635 --> 01:13:26.172
Oh, Phil's working so hard.


01:13:26.173 --> 01:13:28.758
You know... Spring training.


01:13:29.203 --> 01:13:31.979
- We're looking for a house to rent
in case thinks become more permanent.


01:13:31.980 --> 01:13:33.688
You'd like Jacksonville, baby.


01:13:33.689 --> 01:13:34.601
Yeah?


01:13:35.578 --> 01:13:37.154
I'm really liking Forks.


01:13:37.155 --> 01:13:38.053
What?!


01:13:39.861 --> 01:13:41.846
Forks is getting to me.


01:13:41.847 --> 01:13:43.935
Could a guy have anything to do with that?


01:13:46.441 --> 01:13:47.502
Yeah...


01:13:47.503 --> 01:13:50.639
- I knew it! Tell me everything.
What is he? A jock?


01:13:50.640 --> 01:13:53.006
- Indie? I bet he's smart.
Is he smart?


01:13:55.482 --> 01:13:58.053
Mom, can I talk to you later?


01:13:58.054 --> 01:14:00.405
- Come on, we gotta talk boys!
Are you being safe?


01:14:06.200 --> 01:14:07.628
How did you get in here?


01:14:08.760 --> 01:14:10.229
The window.


01:14:10.881 --> 01:14:12.231
Do you do that a lot?


01:14:14.073 --> 01:14:15.946
Just the past couple months.


01:14:20.350 --> 01:14:22.014
I like watching you sleep...


01:14:22.015 --> 01:14:23.191
It's, um...


01:14:23.700 --> 01:14:28.235
Kind of fascinating to me.


01:14:31.470 --> 01:14:33.846
Um, I just want to try one thing...


01:14:35.405 --> 01:14:37.258
Stay very still.


01:14:44.250 --> 01:14:45.886
Don't move...


01:15:30.055 --> 01:15:30.997
Stop!


01:15:33.963 --> 01:15:35.112
I'm sorry...


01:15:38.392 --> 01:15:39.908
I'm stronger than I thought.


01:15:40.657 --> 01:15:43.143
Yeah... I wish I could say the same.


01:15:48.372 --> 01:15:50.381
I can never lose control with you.


01:15:57.100 --> 01:15:58.267
Hey, don't go...


01:16:46.690 --> 01:16:47.820
Hey, I got you another one.


01:16:48.213 --> 01:16:49.370
Thanks.


01:16:49.371 --> 01:16:51.051
I have a date with Edward Cullen.


01:16:54.062 --> 01:16:56.040
He's a little old for you, isn't he?


01:16:57.128 --> 01:17:00.432
No... He's a junior, I'm a junior.


01:17:01.581 --> 01:17:03.044
I thought you liked the Cullens.


01:17:04.376 --> 01:17:06.638
I thought you didn't like
any of the boys in town.


01:17:07.164 --> 01:17:09.288
Edward doesn't live in town...


01:17:10.103 --> 01:17:10.950
Technically.


01:17:14.272 --> 01:17:15.742
He's right outside.


01:17:16.606 --> 01:17:17.518
He is?


01:17:17.907 --> 01:17:20.759
- Yeah, he wanted to meet you...
Officially.


01:17:23.234 --> 01:17:24.150
Alright...


01:17:24.151 --> 01:17:25.995
Bring him in.


01:17:27.148 --> 01:17:30.000
Could you be nice?


01:17:30.249 --> 01:17:31.594
He is important.


01:17:43.565 --> 01:17:47.551
- Chief Swan... I want to formally
introduce myself. I'm Edward Cullen.


01:17:48.410 --> 01:17:49.713
Hi, Edward.


01:17:50.809 --> 01:17:52.341
Bella won't be out too late tonight.


01:17:52.342 --> 01:17:54.367
She's just gonna play
baseball with my family.


01:17:54.541 --> 01:17:55.368
Baseball?


01:17:55.369 --> 01:17:57.222
Yes sir, that's the plan.


01:17:57.467 --> 01:17:59.141
Bella's gonna play baseball?


01:18:01.045 --> 01:18:02.986
Well, good luck with that...


01:18:02.987 --> 01:18:04.000
I'll take good care of her, I promise.


01:18:10.661 --> 01:18:12.251
Hey... You still got that pepper spray?


01:18:12.888 --> 01:18:14.259
Yeah, dad.


01:18:19.751 --> 01:18:21.720
Since when do vampires like baseball?


01:18:22.597 --> 01:18:24.848
Well, it's the American pastime.


01:18:25.259 --> 01:18:29.312
- And... There's a thunderstorm coming.
It's the only time we can play.


01:18:29.575 --> 01:18:30.701
You'll see why.


01:18:44.914 --> 01:18:46.758
- I'm glad you're here...
We need an umpire.


01:18:47.248 --> 01:18:48.735
She thinks we cheat.


01:18:48.736 --> 01:18:49.808
I know you cheat.


01:18:51.520 --> 01:18:53.721
Call them as you see them, Bella.


01:18:53.722 --> 01:18:54.620
Okay.


01:19:04.407 --> 01:19:06.089
It's time...


01:19:14.217 --> 01:19:16.448
Okay, now I see why you need the thunder.


01:19:21.776 --> 01:19:23.224
That's gonna be a homerun, right?


01:19:24.278 --> 01:19:26.103
Edward's very fast.


01:19:39.066 --> 01:19:39.839
You're out.


01:19:39.840 --> 01:19:41.122
Out! Whoo!


01:19:42.395 --> 01:19:44.980
Babe, come on! It's just a game.


01:19:50.500 --> 01:19:51.629
Nice, kid...


01:20:32.498 --> 01:20:33.950
My monkey-man...


01:20:48.556 --> 01:20:49.455
Stop!


01:21:06.275 --> 01:21:08.013
They were leaving, then they heard us.


01:21:08.808 --> 01:21:09.623
Let's go.


01:21:09.624 --> 01:21:10.881
It's too late.


01:21:12.412 --> 01:21:13.524
Get your hair up.


01:21:15.258 --> 01:21:18.241
- Like that would help. I could
smell her from across the field.


01:21:25.022 --> 01:21:27.082
- I shouldn't have brought you here.
I'm so sorry...


01:21:27.083 --> 01:21:27.942
What?


01:21:27.943 --> 01:21:29.800
Just be quiet and stand behind me.


01:21:52.020 --> 01:21:53.884
I believe this belongs to you.


01:21:57.562 --> 01:21:58.556
Thank you.


01:21:58.750 --> 01:21:59.725
I'm Laurent...


01:22:00.839 --> 01:22:02.208
And this is Victoria...


01:22:04.227 --> 01:22:05.230
And James.


01:22:06.500 --> 01:22:07.770
I'm Carlisle...


01:22:07.805 --> 01:22:08.687
This is my family.


01:22:11.024 --> 01:22:11.781
Hello.


01:22:12.385 --> 01:22:15.865
- I'm afraid your hunting activities
have caused something of a mess for us.


01:22:15.991 --> 01:22:17.301
Our apologies.


01:22:18.179 --> 01:22:20.765
- We didn't realize the territory
had been claimed.


01:22:20.766 --> 01:22:24.269
- Yes, well...
We maintain a permanent residence nearby.


01:22:26.014 --> 01:22:27.166
Really?


01:22:29.284 --> 01:22:32.729
Well, we won't be a problem anymore.


01:22:33.715 --> 01:22:35.089
We were just passing through.


01:22:35.090 --> 01:22:38.331
- The humans were tracking us
but we lead them east.


01:22:38.332 --> 01:22:40.053
You should be safe.


01:22:40.686 --> 01:22:41.666
Excellent.


01:22:42.432 --> 01:22:44.184
So...


01:22:44.219 --> 01:22:46.316
Could you use three more players?


01:22:48.809 --> 01:22:51.182
Oh, come on. Just one game.


01:22:51.883 --> 01:22:52.652
Sure,


01:22:52.687 --> 01:22:53.659
why not?


01:22:53.694 --> 01:22:54.998
Three of us were leaving...


01:22:55.033 --> 01:22:56.129
You can take their place.


01:22:56.164 --> 01:22:57.921
You go first.


01:22:57.956 --> 01:23:00.932
I'm the one with the wicked curve-ball.


01:23:01.200 --> 01:23:03.305
Well, I think we can handle that.


01:23:05.408 --> 01:23:06.816
We shall see...


01:23:27.073 --> 01:23:28.541
You brought a snack.


01:23:31.305 --> 01:23:32.524
You're human?


01:23:36.204 --> 01:23:37.404
The girl is with us.


01:23:38.269 --> 01:23:39.865
I think it best if you leave.


01:23:44.197 --> 01:23:45.771
I can see the game is over.


01:23:46.000 --> 01:23:47.346
We'll go now.


01:23:50.800 --> 01:23:51.778
James...


01:24:04.372 --> 01:24:07.420
Get Bella out of here... Go.


01:24:18.170 --> 01:24:19.914
Okay, I've got it! I've got it! I'm alright.


01:24:22.890 --> 01:24:24.552
What? Now James is coming after me?


01:24:35.183 --> 01:24:36.702
Listen to me, James is a tracker.


01:24:36.703 --> 01:24:38.994
The hunt is his obsession. I read his mind.


01:24:38.995 --> 01:24:40.870
My reaction at the field set him off.


01:24:40.871 --> 01:24:44.149
I just made this his
most exciting game ever.


01:24:44.338 --> 01:24:45.803
He's never gonna stop.


01:24:45.822 --> 01:24:47.123
- What should we do?
- We have to kill him.


01:24:47.124 --> 01:24:48.821
Rip him apart and burn the pieces.


01:24:49.366 --> 01:24:50.601
Where are we going?


01:24:50.602 --> 01:24:51.673
Away from Forks...


01:24:51.674 --> 01:24:53.201
We'll get a ferry to Vancouver.


01:24:53.202 --> 01:24:55.424
- I have to go home, now!
You should take me home.


01:24:55.425 --> 01:24:56.686
You can't go home.


01:24:58.028 --> 01:25:01.331
- He's just gonna trace your scent there...
It's the first place he's gonna look.


01:25:01.332 --> 01:25:02.125
But my dad is there...


01:25:02.160 --> 01:25:03.051
It doesn't matter!


01:25:03.052 --> 01:25:05.343
- Yes, it does!
He could get killed because of us.


01:25:07.645 --> 01:25:09.570
Just let me get you out
of here first, alright?


01:25:09.571 --> 01:25:11.031
It's my dad! We have to go back.


01:25:12.010 --> 01:25:14.291
We'll figure how to lead the
tracker away somehow... I don't know!


01:25:14.292 --> 01:25:15.512
But we have to do something.


01:25:21.885 --> 01:25:23.459
Edward, I said leave me alone!


01:25:23.460 --> 01:25:24.751
Bella, don't do this, please...


01:25:24.752 --> 01:25:26.286
It's over, get out!


01:25:26.867 --> 01:25:27.866
Hey... Hey hey!


01:25:27.867 --> 01:25:29.665
Bella, what's going on?


01:25:30.716 --> 01:25:32.008
I just gotta get out of here.


01:25:32.009 --> 01:25:33.269
I'm leaving... Now!


01:25:39.942 --> 01:25:40.809
Bella?


01:25:41.846 --> 01:25:43.582
What am I gonna say to him?


01:25:44.000 --> 01:25:45.465
I can't hurt him.


01:25:45.500 --> 01:25:48.127
- Bella, what's going on?
- You'll just have to.


01:25:49.715 --> 01:25:50.997
I'll be down at the truck.


01:25:57.095 --> 01:25:58.464
Did he hurt you?


01:25:59.486 --> 01:26:01.219
No.


01:26:02.869 --> 01:26:04.860
Break up with you or something?


01:26:05.196 --> 01:26:07.170
No, I... I broke up with him.


01:26:09.619 --> 01:26:11.129
I thought you liked him.


01:26:14.113 --> 01:26:16.030
Yeah, that's just why I have to leave.


01:26:16.031 --> 01:26:18.583
I don't want this, I have to go home.


01:26:20.599 --> 01:26:23.690
- Home...?
Your mom is not even in Phoenix.


01:26:24.862 --> 01:26:26.423
- She'll come home.
I'll call her from the road.


01:26:26.424 --> 01:26:28.452
You don't have to drive home right now.


01:26:28.453 --> 01:26:30.473
You can sleep on it.


01:26:31.139 --> 01:26:33.072
If you still feel like going in the
morning, I'll take you to the airport.


01:26:33.073 --> 01:26:36.430
- No, I want to drive, it will
give more time to think.


01:26:36.431 --> 01:26:39.912
- If I get really tired, I'll pull
into a motel... I promise.


01:26:39.913 --> 01:26:42.534
- Look, Bella... I know I'm not that
much fun to be around...


01:26:42.535 --> 01:26:44.903
But I can change that...


01:26:45.441 --> 01:26:46.968
We can do more stuff together.


01:26:50.206 --> 01:26:53.717
- Like what?
Like watch baseball on the flatscreen?


01:26:54.641 --> 01:26:56.630
- Eat at the dinner every night?
Steak and Cobbler?


01:26:57.437 --> 01:26:58.942
Dad, that's you... That's not me.


01:27:02.746 --> 01:27:06.346
Bella, come on. I just... got you back.


01:27:09.975 --> 01:27:11.586
Yeah, you know... If I don't get out now,


01:27:11.944 --> 01:27:14.154
I'm just gonna be just stuck here like mom.


01:27:39.319 --> 01:27:41.219
Your father's gonna forgive you.


01:27:43.160 --> 01:27:45.296
Why don't you let me drive?


01:27:51.359 --> 01:27:52.719
He won't.


01:27:53.951 --> 01:27:55.419
You should have seen his face...


01:27:57.657 --> 01:28:01.020
- I told him the same thing that my
mom told him when she was leaving him.


01:28:01.021 --> 01:28:03.049
It was the only way he'd let you go.


01:28:06.301 --> 01:28:10.147
- Just don't worry about him now.
He's safe. The tracker's following us.


01:28:14.310 --> 01:28:15.439
It's just Emmett.


01:28:18.153 --> 01:28:19.988
Alice is in the car behind us.


01:28:42.023 --> 01:28:43.748
Wait!


01:28:44.358 --> 01:28:46.801
- He came to warn us...
About James.


01:28:46.802 --> 01:28:48.333
This isn't my fight and...


01:28:48.334 --> 01:28:50.401
I've grown tired of his games.


01:28:51.411 --> 01:28:54.217
But he's got unparalleled
senses, absolutely lethal.


01:28:54.218 --> 01:28:56.694
- I've never seen anything like him
in my three hundred years.


01:28:57.281 --> 01:29:01.061
- And the woman, Victoria...
Don't underestimate her.


01:29:06.172 --> 01:29:08.426
- I've had to fight our kind before.
We're not easy to kill.


01:29:08.427 --> 01:29:09.269
But not impossible.


01:29:10.696 --> 01:29:12.812
We'll rip him apart and burn the pieces.


01:29:12.813 --> 01:29:15.004
I don't relish the thought
of killing another creature.


01:29:15.005 --> 01:29:16.726
Even a sadistic one like James.


01:29:17.500 --> 01:29:18.994
What if he kills one of us first?


01:29:19.248 --> 01:29:22.204
- I'm gonna run Bella south and then
lead the tracker away from here.


01:29:22.205 --> 01:29:25.454
- No, Edward. James knows you'd
never leave Bella. He'll follow you.


01:29:25.502 --> 01:29:27.792
- I'll go with Bella.
Jasper and I will drive her south.


01:29:28.447 --> 01:29:29.912
I'll keep her safe, Edward.


01:29:29.913 --> 01:29:31.375
Can you keep your thoughts to yourself?


01:29:31.376 --> 01:29:32.272
Yes.


01:29:36.289 --> 01:29:39.204
Rosalie... Esme...


01:29:39.205 --> 01:29:42.356
Could you put these on so...


01:29:42.357 --> 01:29:44.109
The tracker will pick up Bella's scent?


01:29:45.928 --> 01:29:47.793
Why? What is she to me?


01:29:48.415 --> 01:29:52.873
- Rosalie... Bella is with Edward.
She is part of this family now.


01:29:55.190 --> 01:29:56.634
And we protect our family.


01:30:15.098 --> 01:30:19.935
If anything happens, I just...


01:30:19.936 --> 01:30:21.478
Nothing's gonna happen.


01:30:21.915 --> 01:30:24.028
There's seven of us against two of them.


01:30:24.661 --> 01:30:27.200
- And when everything's done,
I'm gonna come back and get you.


01:30:28.429 --> 01:30:29.403
Yeah.


01:30:30.493 --> 01:30:32.914
Bella, you are my life now.


01:30:49.998 --> 01:30:52.054
Hey, mom. It's me again.


01:30:52.055 --> 01:30:54.126
- Um, you must have let your phone
die or something...


01:30:54.127 --> 01:30:58.542
- I'm not in Forks but everything's okay
and I'll explain it later.


01:31:05.395 --> 01:31:07.013
Rose, among the three.


01:31:09.523 --> 01:31:12.852
That's good.


01:31:58.452 --> 01:32:00.445
What is it? What did you see?


01:32:12.162 --> 01:32:13.933
He figured it out.


01:32:13.934 --> 01:32:17.051
The tracker. He just changed course.


01:32:18.722 --> 01:32:19.884
Where will it take him, Alice?


01:32:19.885 --> 01:32:22.096
- Mirrors...
A room full of mirrors.


01:32:26.684 --> 01:32:28.935
- Edward said the visions weren't
always certain.


01:32:28.936 --> 01:32:32.418
- She sees the course people are
on while they're on it.


01:32:32.419 --> 01:32:34.312
If they change their
minds, the vision changes.


01:32:34.313 --> 01:32:38.900
- So, the course that the tracker's on
now is gonna lead him to... A ballet studio?


01:32:40.118 --> 01:32:41.469
You've been here?


01:32:41.470 --> 01:32:43.718
I took lessons as a kid.


01:32:44.143 --> 01:32:45.929
The school I went to had
an arch just like that.


01:32:45.930 --> 01:32:47.228
Was your school here in Phoenix?


01:32:47.229 --> 01:32:48.468
Yeah.


01:32:50.090 --> 01:32:50.909
Edward, you okay?


01:32:50.910 --> 01:32:53.534
- We've lost the tracker.
The woman's still in the area.


01:32:53.535 --> 01:32:56.480
- Rosalie and Esme have gone back
to Forks to protect your father.


01:32:56.481 --> 01:32:57.644
I'm coming to get you.


01:32:57.645 --> 01:33:00.928
Then you and I are gonna go somewhere...


01:33:01.535 --> 01:33:02.437
Alone.


01:33:02.438 --> 01:33:04.036
And the others will keep hunting.


01:33:04.037 --> 01:33:06.982
I'll do whatever it takes
to make you safe again.


01:33:18.872 --> 01:33:21.313
Hey, mom! I'm glad you got my message.


01:33:21.314 --> 01:33:22.781
What are you doing home?


01:33:22.782 --> 01:33:25.623
Bella! Bella, Bella?! Where are you?


01:33:26.257 --> 01:33:28.060
Calm down, everything's fine.


01:33:28.200 --> 01:33:29.100
Bella!


01:33:29.549 --> 01:33:33.202
- I'll explain everything later...
Mom, are you alright?


01:33:33.203 --> 01:33:36.529
- Forks High School doesn't protect
the student's privacy very well.


01:33:37.358 --> 01:33:41.179
- It was just too easy for Victoria
to find your previous address.


01:33:41.180 --> 01:33:43.543
It's a nice house you have here.


01:33:43.544 --> 01:33:45.898
I was prepared to wait for you.


01:33:45.899 --> 01:33:48.502
But then mom came home after she received...


01:33:48.503 --> 01:33:50.479
A very worried call from your dad.


01:33:50.480 --> 01:33:53.685
It all worked out quite well.


01:33:55.103 --> 01:33:56.977
Don't touch her! Don't..!


01:33:56.978 --> 01:33:59.020
You can still save her.


01:33:59.532 --> 01:34:01.981
But you're gonna have to
get away from your friends.


01:34:01.982 --> 01:34:03.403
Can you handle that?


01:34:03.884 --> 01:34:05.182
Where should I meet you?


01:34:07.734 --> 01:34:09.619
How about your old ballet studio?


01:34:10.561 --> 01:34:12.863
And I'd know if you bring anyone along...


01:34:15.508 --> 01:34:18.131
Poor mommy would pay the
price for that mistake.


01:34:35.326 --> 01:34:37.616
I'd never given much
thought to how I would die...


01:34:39.578 --> 01:34:41.725
But dying in the place of someone I love,


01:34:41.760 --> 01:34:43.318
seems like a good way to go.


01:34:51.833 --> 01:34:56.012
I can't bring myself to regret the decisions
that brought me face to face with dead.


01:34:56.013 --> 01:34:58.051
They also brought me to Edward.


01:35:31.000 --> 01:35:32.500
Mom.


01:35:32.501 --> 01:35:33.300
Mom!


01:35:56.000 --> 01:35:57.960
That's my favorite part.


01:35:58.863 --> 01:36:01.256
You were a stubborn child, weren't you?


01:36:03.455 --> 01:36:05.159
She's not even here...


01:36:08.700 --> 01:36:12.649
- Sorry...
But you really made it too easy.


01:36:13.361 --> 01:36:17.106
so... To make things more entertaining,


01:36:17.107 --> 01:36:19.699
we are gonna make a little
film of our time together.


01:36:21.689 --> 01:36:25.028
- I borrowed this from your house.
I hope you don't mind.


01:36:25.357 --> 01:36:26.270
Okay...


01:36:26.294 --> 01:36:30.856
- And...
Action!


01:36:33.016 --> 01:36:34.786
That will break Edward's little heart.


01:36:35.900 --> 01:36:37.635
Edward has nothing to do with this!


01:36:37.636 --> 01:36:43.594
He does... His rage will leave
for more interesting sporthings...


01:36:43.895 --> 01:36:46.157
Than this feeble attempt to protect you.


01:36:47.042 --> 01:36:48.879
And let's continue.


01:37:04.058 --> 01:37:08.368
Beautiful... Very visually dynamic.


01:37:10.251 --> 01:37:12.491
I chose my stage well.


01:37:17.667 --> 01:37:20.407
It's too bad he didn't have
the strength to turn you.


01:37:21.710 --> 01:37:24.441
Instead he kept you this
fragile little human.


01:37:24.442 --> 01:37:25.893
It's cruel, really.


01:37:30.741 --> 01:37:32.625
Tell him to avenge you.


01:37:33.637 --> 01:37:35.419
Tell him to avenge you! Tell him!


01:37:35.420 --> 01:37:36.368
Edward, don't!


01:37:36.900 --> 01:37:38.600
Tell him!


01:37:50.840 --> 01:37:54.321
- You're alone...
'cause you're faster than the others...


01:37:56.173 --> 01:37:57.841
But not stronger.


01:37:59.583 --> 01:38:01.859
I'm strong enough to kill you.


01:38:08.924 --> 01:38:10.112
I'm sorry.


01:39:13.697 --> 01:39:15.500
Bella, Bella! It's okay.


01:39:15.501 --> 01:39:17.240
Son...


01:39:17.428 --> 01:39:20.143
Enough! Remember who you are.


01:39:26.531 --> 01:39:28.422
Bella needs you.


01:39:30.705 --> 01:39:31.915
Oh God.


01:39:35.789 --> 01:39:37.759
Carlisle! The blood...


01:39:37.760 --> 01:39:39.321
Your brothers will take care of it.


01:39:39.980 --> 01:39:41.753
Start the fire with the floor boards.


01:39:43.807 --> 01:39:45.856
- Alice!
- Alice, go.


01:39:55.562 --> 01:39:58.029
- Her femoral artery has been savaged.
She's losing too much blood.


01:39:58.030 --> 01:39:59.883
No, no, my hand... Is burning!


01:40:01.523 --> 01:40:02.496
It's the venom.


01:40:04.235 --> 01:40:06.373
You have to make a choice
to prevent the change happen.


01:40:07.600 --> 01:40:10.152
No...


01:40:10.153 --> 01:40:10.922
No!


01:40:12.568 --> 01:40:14.644
It's gonna happen, Edward. I've seen it.


01:40:14.645 --> 01:40:16.452
It doesn't have to be that way.


01:40:16.453 --> 01:40:18.033
She'd still have what she has.


01:40:18.034 --> 01:40:19.501
Make me a tourniquet with your belt.


01:40:19.502 --> 01:40:22.167
Carlisle, what's my other option?


01:40:22.843 --> 01:40:24.385
Tie it above my hands.


01:40:24.386 --> 01:40:26.623
Carlisle!


01:40:28.250 --> 01:40:29.857
Go.


01:40:34.454 --> 01:40:35.808
To try to suck the venom out.


01:40:35.809 --> 01:40:37.222
You know I won't be able to stop.


01:40:37.223 --> 01:40:39.110
Then find the will... To stop.


01:40:40.174 --> 01:40:43.259
But choose. She only has minutes left.


01:40:46.000 --> 01:40:47.569
I can't make you go away, Bella.


01:40:50.600 --> 01:40:52.367
But I'll make it go away.


01:41:10.959 --> 01:41:12.461
Edward, stop!


01:41:12.462 --> 01:41:14.553
The blood is clean, you're killing her.


01:41:15.686 --> 01:41:18.792
Edward, stop!


01:41:19.829 --> 01:41:23.576
Stop. Find the will.


01:41:48.709 --> 01:41:51.897
Dead is peaceful... Easy...


01:41:59.100 --> 01:42:00.649
Life is harder.


01:42:06.400 --> 01:42:07.705
Bella?


01:42:09.800 --> 01:42:11.100
Baby?


01:42:12.800 --> 01:42:14.000
Bella?


01:42:15.100 --> 01:42:16.100
Mom...


01:42:16.300 --> 01:42:17.800
Hey...


01:42:18.052 --> 01:42:22.475
Where is he? Where's... Where is Edward?


01:42:22.476 --> 01:42:24.124
He's asleep.


01:42:25.379 --> 01:42:26.946
He never leaves.


01:42:26.947 --> 01:42:29.136
And your dad is down at the cafeteria.


01:42:30.475 --> 01:42:32.578
What happened?


01:42:32.579 --> 01:42:34.864
Well, when you fell you broke your leg.


01:42:36.341 --> 01:42:38.240
And you lost a lot of blood.


01:42:39.153 --> 01:42:41.217
You don't remember any of this, do you?


01:42:43.579 --> 01:42:47.351
- Edward came down with his dad to
try to convince to come back to Forks.


01:42:47.462 --> 01:42:50.352
- So you went over to their hotel
and you tripped...


01:42:51.444 --> 01:42:53.647
And fell down two flights of stairs...


01:42:54.338 --> 01:42:56.172
And through a window!


01:43:03.008 --> 01:43:04.279
Yeah, it sounds like me.


01:43:04.280 --> 01:43:06.845
Oh, honey. I'm so sorry.


01:43:10.696 --> 01:43:11.607
It's Phil.


01:43:12.229 --> 01:43:14.412
He's so worried about you.


01:43:16.312 --> 01:43:17.627
You're texting...?


01:43:17.628 --> 01:43:19.616
Finally, yeah.


01:43:20.882 --> 01:43:22.988
I told him to stay down in Florida.


01:43:22.989 --> 01:43:26.869
- Oh, honey. You are gonna love Jacksonville.
- It's sunny everyday day.


01:43:27.747 --> 01:43:30.391
- And we found the cutest little house
and you've got your own bathroom.


01:43:30.774 --> 01:43:32.303
No, Mom. I still wanna live in Forks.


01:43:33.789 --> 01:43:34.837
What?


01:43:35.431 --> 01:43:36.862
I wanna live in Forks.


01:43:36.863 --> 01:43:40.457
Well, okay. We'll talk about it.


01:43:41.043 --> 01:43:43.438
Do you mind getting dad?


01:43:44.597 --> 01:43:47.735
I have to talk to him. Apologize.


01:43:47.996 --> 01:43:49.020
Okay, baby.


01:43:49.021 --> 01:43:50.512
I'll go get him.


01:43:50.900 --> 01:43:53.170
And I'll go get a nurse, okay?


01:43:53.205 --> 01:43:54.209
Okay.


01:44:07.177 --> 01:44:08.903
What happened? Where is James?


01:44:10.718 --> 01:44:13.714
We took care of him.


01:44:18.780 --> 01:44:21.449
And the woman, Victoria, she ran off.


01:44:22.161 --> 01:44:24.006
I'm alive because of you.


01:44:24.387 --> 01:44:26.986
No, you're in here because of me.


01:44:28.311 --> 01:44:31.968
The worst part of it was...


01:44:31.969 --> 01:44:34.434
I thought I wasn't gonna be able to stop.


01:44:34.969 --> 01:44:36.330
You did stop.


01:44:37.751 --> 01:44:40.488
Bella, you gotta go to Jacksonville,


01:44:40.489 --> 01:44:42.364
so I can't hurt you anymore.


01:44:44.142 --> 01:44:45.454
What?


01:44:49.500 --> 01:44:52.004
No, no!


01:44:53.065 --> 01:44:57.158
- I don't even know what you're...?
What are you talking about?


01:44:57.159 --> 01:45:00.148
- You want me to go away?
I can't just leave you...


01:45:00.149 --> 01:45:01.813
I know.


01:45:04.273 --> 01:45:07.070
We can't be apart. You can't leave me.


01:45:07.449 --> 01:45:09.645
I'm here.


01:45:13.232 --> 01:45:18.438
- Okay. You just can't just say stuff
like that to me. Ever.


01:45:22.596 --> 01:45:25.951
Where else am I gonna go?


01:46:15.131 --> 01:46:16.525
Alice lent me the dress.


01:46:17.835 --> 01:46:18.924
The cast is...


01:46:20.448 --> 01:46:21.824
Perfect.


01:46:24.487 --> 01:46:26.420
I'll take care of her, Chief Swan.


01:46:27.901 --> 01:46:29.322
Uhu. I've heard that before.


01:46:35.155 --> 01:46:40.174
- Hey, Bells. I put a new can of
Pepper spray on your bag.


01:46:40.574 --> 01:46:41.534
Dad...


01:46:42.577 --> 01:46:43.735
And, um...


01:46:46.665 --> 01:46:48.317
You look beautiful.


01:46:50.172 --> 01:46:51.109
Thanks.


01:46:52.946 --> 01:46:54.085
See you.


01:47:01.600 --> 01:47:04.500
Hey. Be right back.


01:47:06.696 --> 01:47:07.925
Bella.


01:47:08.300 --> 01:47:09.400
Jacob.


01:47:09.700 --> 01:47:11.300
Hey!


01:47:11.466 --> 01:47:12.670
Nice.


01:47:12.671 --> 01:47:13.940
You too.


01:47:14.369 --> 01:47:16.652
- Are you crashing the prom or something?
Did you come with a date?


01:47:18.078 --> 01:47:19.967
No.


01:47:23.251 --> 01:47:25.648
My dad paid me to come talk to you.


01:47:26.541 --> 01:47:27.700
Twenty bucks.


01:47:27.701 --> 01:47:29.192
Let's hear it.


01:47:30.760 --> 01:47:32.251
Just don't get mad, okay?


01:47:34.509 --> 01:47:36.704
He wants you to break
up with your boyfriend.


01:47:37.298 --> 01:47:40.506
He's just... He said,


01:47:40.507 --> 01:47:41.952
quote:


01:47:41.953 --> 01:47:43.781
"We'll be watching you. "


01:47:45.608 --> 01:47:47.400
- Okay. Well, tell him thanks.
- Okay...


01:47:48.664 --> 01:47:49.900
- And to pay up.
- Okay.


01:47:50.400 --> 01:47:52.800
- Oh, let me help you.
- Jacob.


01:47:52.900 --> 01:47:54.975
I'll take it from here.


01:47:58.756 --> 01:48:00.531
I guess I'll see you around, Bella.


01:48:11.335 --> 01:48:14.781
- I leave you alone for two minutes
and the wolves descend.


01:48:22.100 --> 01:48:23.888
I can't believe you're making me do this.


01:48:23.889 --> 01:48:24.849
Smile.


01:48:46.146 --> 01:48:47.977
Wow! You are really trying to kill me.


01:48:48.894 --> 01:48:50.693
Prom is an important rite of passage.


01:48:50.694 --> 01:48:52.307
I don't want you to miss anything.


01:49:21.300 --> 01:49:22.500
Bella!


01:49:26.000 --> 01:49:27.133
You wanna go?


01:49:27.134 --> 01:49:28.112
Yeah.


01:49:36.513 --> 01:49:37.584
Shall we?


01:49:39.163 --> 01:49:40.294
You're serious?


01:49:41.845 --> 01:49:42.825
Oh, why not?


01:49:58.817 --> 01:50:00.352
See? You're dancing.


01:50:02.200 --> 01:50:03.321
At Prom...


01:50:24.068 --> 01:50:26.071
Edward, why did you save me?


01:50:27.000 --> 01:50:28.736
If you just had let the venom spread...


01:50:29.533 --> 01:50:31.429
I could be like you right now.


01:50:33.955 --> 01:50:35.553
You don't know what you're saying.


01:50:37.055 --> 01:50:38.477
You don't want this.


01:50:38.478 --> 01:50:40.816
- I want you.
Always.


01:50:46.905 --> 01:50:49.175
I'm not gonna end your life for you.


01:50:49.427 --> 01:50:52.150
I'm dying... Already.


01:50:53.543 --> 01:50:58.011
Every second I get closer... Older.


01:50:58.870 --> 01:51:00.614
That's the way it's supposed to be.


01:51:02.015 --> 01:51:05.096
- Alice said that she saw me like you.
I heard her.


01:51:05.460 --> 01:51:06.401
Her visions change.


01:51:07.108 --> 01:51:08.856
Yeah, but someday people decide.


01:51:10.117 --> 01:51:11.719
I've decided.


01:51:15.276 --> 01:51:17.090
Is that what you dream about?


01:51:17.874 --> 01:51:19.201
Becoming a monster?


01:51:23.135 --> 01:51:25.300
I dream about being with you forever.


01:51:25.301 --> 01:51:27.272
Forever...


01:51:32.546 --> 01:51:34.826
Are you ready right now?


01:51:36.353 --> 01:51:37.679
Yes.


01:51:54.687 --> 01:51:59.497
- Is it not enough just to have a
long and happy life with me?


01:52:06.448 --> 01:52:07.762
Yeah.


01:52:09.854 --> 01:52:11.014
For now.


01:52:39.755 --> 01:52:41.718
No one will surrender tonight.


01:52:42.700 --> 01:52:44.973
But I won’t give in.


01:52:46.126 --> 01:52:47.494
I know what I want.


01:52:48.900 --> 01:52:49.950
EDiT / ResYncH


